                "\n",
                "Two numbers, and they answer different questions:\n",
                "\n",
                "- **Score** - of the checks we ran, how closely the practice was followed.\n",
                "- **Coverage** - how many of the checks we could run at all.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Low coverage is our gap, not the workspace's.** A check with no result is one we could not run - some are not written yet, most need a source system tables do not expose, or judgment a query cannot make. Low coverage means we looked at less, not that the workspace did less.\n",
                "\n",
                "*NOT AVAILABLE* means nothing in that category could be measured.\n"
              ]
